RavenGun-wijziging 0001 op OpenParrot: de lader vraagt CONTEXT_FLOATING_POINT niet meer aan (Wine-fix).
ContextFlags 0x1001F -> 0x10017. Waarom: docs/decisions.md ("Eigen OpenParrot-lader en -kern"), docs/per-game-patches.md.
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later (zelfde licentie als OpenParrot)

diff -ruN a/OpenParrotLoader/src/main.cpp b/OpenParrotLoader/src/main.cpp
--- a/OpenParrotLoader/src/main.cpp
+++ b/OpenParrotLoader/src/main.cpp
@@ -871,7 +871,17 @@
 	}
 	else
 	{
-		mycontext.ContextFlags = 0x00010000 + 1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 0x10;
+		// RavenGun modification (Wine): CONTEXT_FLOATING_POINT (0x8) is deliberately NOT requested any more.
+		// This one context (mycontext) is used for every GetThreadContext/SetThreadContext call below
+		// (RunTo and LoadHookDLL), and the loader only needs the control, integer, segment and debug
+		// registers to move EIP/RIP. Under Wine, SetThreadContext with CONTEXT_FLOATING_POINT but without
+		// CONTEXT_EXTENDED_REGISTERS writes an all-zero MXCSR into the game's main thread, which unmasks every
+		// SSE exception; the game then dies with c00002b5 (STATUS_FLOAT_MULTIPLE_TRAPS) on the first inexact
+		// conversion. The loader only reads the floating point state and writes the same values back, so
+		// leaving it out changes nothing on Windows.
+		// Flags: CONTEXT_i386 | CONTROL | INTEGER | SEGMENTS | DEBUG_REGISTERS
+		// (was 0x00010000 + 1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 0x10 = 0x1001F, now 0x10017).
+		mycontext.ContextFlags = 0x00010000 + 1 + 2 + 4 + 0x10;
 		GetThreadContext(pi.hThread, &mycontext);
 
 		PROCESS_BASIC_INFORMATION pbi = { 0 };
